sdata> -- REPL parity for UNSET /ALL: without NEW /PROGRAM first, the still-queued
sdata> -- SET A=1/SET B=2 would replay on this second RUN (REPL's Active_Program_Vec
sdata> -- persists across RUN -- see RUN's row in design.md) and silently resurrect
sdata> -- A right after UNSET /ALL removed it. NEW /PROGRAM discards the queued
sdata> -- program first, giving REPL the same result as batch.
sdata> NEW
sdata> USE MOCK
Generating mock data...
sdata> SET A = 1
sdata> SET B = 2
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 3 records and 3 variables processed.
sdata> NEW /PROGRAM
sdata> UNSET /ALL
sdata> PRINT A
sdata> RUN
Error: undefined variable "A"
sdata> QUIT
